If length is 1..4, mng_get_long(&chunk[1]) reads chunk[1..4] → heap-buffer-overflow READ of up to 3 bytes past the allocation (for length=1, reads 4 bytes past end; for length=4, reads 1 byte past end).

Wait, actually for length=1, chunk allocated 1 byte; mng_get_long(&chunk[1]) reads bytes chunk[1], chunk[2], chunk[3], chunk[4] — all out of bounds → heap-buffer-overflow read of 4 bytes at offset 1 of a 1-byte region.

